    "field": "Ice shelf dynamics",
    "problem": "Accurate mass-balance estimates for the Antarctic ice sheet are challenged by a lack of reliable data on bottom melting beneath ice shelves, as very few estimates have been made and the process was suspected to be less widespread, hindering understanding of total ice loss.",
    "method": "This study uses glaciological measurements of ice velocity, strain-rates, and thickness along a flow line to compute the mass balance, particle trajectories, and bottom melting rates of the Brunt Ice Shelf by applying principles of mass continuity.",
    "task": "The task is to determine the dynamics of the Brunt Ice Shelf by analyzing field observations of its mass balance, ice movement, strain rates, bottom melting, and calving processes.",
